# Deny everything, then explicitly allow only what the build needs. Keeping the
# build context minimal speeds up `docker build` and stops unrelated file edits
# (docs, IDE state, .git) from invalidating cached layers. It also means a new
# kind of local-only file cannot leak into the image by default.
*

!Directory.Build.props
!Directory.Packages.props
!src/**

# Re-deny build output and local-only files that the src/** allow would otherwise
# pull back in. Excluding bin/obj also keeps generated files (*.AssemblyInfo.cs,
# *.GlobalUsings.g.cs) out of the context so they cannot bust the layer cache.
**/bin
**/obj
**/*.user
**/appsettings.Local*.json
**/secrets.json

# Test projects are never part of a runtime image.
**/*.Tests
